---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/github';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Getting started"
  description="What Semper does, signing in, and image requirements."
  path="/manual/getting-started"
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 3rem">
    <p class="crumb">
      <a href={withBase('/manual')}>← Manual</a>
    </p>
    <h2>Getting started</h2>
    <p class="sub">What the app returns, how accounts work, and which frames you can load.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h3>What it does</h3>
      <p>
        Give Semper one <strong>reference</strong> frame and N <strong>deformed</strong> frames. It
        matches subsets on a grid and returns five fields per frame:
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Unit</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>U</strong>, <strong>V</strong> — displacement</td>
            <td>px</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Exx</strong>, <strong>Eyy</strong>, <strong>Exy</strong> — strain</td>
            <td>mε (millistrain)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="callout">
        Displacements are in <strong>pixels</strong> — there is no scale calibration. Convert to
        physical units yourself. Everything runs on the phone; cloud backup stores results only.
      </div>

      <h3>Getting in</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Sign in with Google or email.</li>
        <li>
          Email passwords need 8+ characters with upper and lower case, a digit, and a special
          character. <strong>Generate secure password</strong> can fill one in.
        </li>
        <li>
          Email sign-up sends a verification link. Open it, then sign in. Until you verify,
          sign-in is refused.
        </li>
        <li>
          New accounts land on <strong>Pending approval</strong>. Support is emailed automatically.
        </li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Request access</strong> if you want to add context.</li>
        <li>
          After approval, tap <strong>Check status</strong>. Nothing polls — the screen never
          updates on its own.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Offline works if you have been approved on this device before. Import, solve, and read
        results work without a network; uploads wait.
      </p>

      <h3>Images it accepts</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Rule</th>
            <th>If broken</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>All frames the same pixel size as the reference</td>
            <td>Blocking error; you cannot run</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>At least one reference + one deformed frame</td>
            <td><strong>Next</strong> stays off</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>At most <em>Max frames</em> (default 50)</td>
            <td>Extras dropped, with a toast</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        <strong>Formats.</strong> PNG and TIFF are best. JPEG works but raises an accuracy warning —
        compression damages the intensity gradients correlation needs. RAW and DNG import only
        through <strong>Files</strong>, not Photos.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Texture check.</strong> On import the app measures your speckle. Weak pattern → a
        warning naming a bigger subset size.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Video.</strong> Pick a video and a sampling sheet opens. Frame 0 becomes the
        reference.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={withBase('/manual/analysis')}>Next: Running an analysis</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={withBase('/manual/faq')}>FAQ</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
